      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 176,
      "text": "MEXICO\nAnnex IV. The Subcontracting Law, Employment, and GDP\nMeasurement\nThe authorities have passed a new legislation restricting the subcontracting of the workforce in 2021.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 176,
      "end_char": 375,
      "text": "This annex reports that a large share of workers who used to be subcontracted transitioned to direct\nemployment status. This has triggered a large decline in the production of those services sectors\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 375,
      "end_char": 590,
      "text": "providing support to business. However, this may not reflect a reduction of activity as part of the value\nadded that used to be generated in these sectors is now generated in the sectors employing workers\ndirectly.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 590,
      "end_char": 769,
      "text": "1. Labor subcontracting in Mexico grew rapidly in the past two decades, from 6 percent\nof total employment in 2003 to 15 percent in 2018 in Mexico. According to the 2019 economic\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 769,
      "end_char": 995,
      "text": "census, subcontracted workers accounted for more than 40 percent of employment in utilities and\nfor 36 percent in financial services.\n2. In April 2021, the authorities enacted new legislation restricting the subcontracting of\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 995,
      "end_char": 1184,
      "text": "the workforce, with the aim of preventing the violation of labor law and tax evasion. The new\nlaw bans service firms from providing employees to be supervised and managed by a third-party,\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1184,
      "end_char": 1387,
      "text": "while it still allows subcontracting of services if the employees are monitored by the firm providing\nthe service.1 The legislation also tightened registration and reporting requirements. Non-compliance\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1387,
      "end_char": 1625,
      "text": "with this new subcontracting law became a criminal offence.\nManufacturing Sector Retail Trade\n(Millions of workers) (Millions of workers)\n5\nOutsourcinglaw compliance deadline 7\n4.5 Outsourcinglaw compliance deadline\n4 6\n3.5 5\n3 4\n2.5\n3\n2\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1625,
      "end_char": 1830,
      "text": "1.5 2\n1 1\n0.5 0\n0\nDirect employment Subcontracted workers Direct employment Subcontracted workers\nSource: INEGI.\n3. As a result, a sizeable share of the workforce transitioned from a subcontract to direct\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1830,
      "end_char": 2017,
      "text": "employment status in the second and third quarter of 2021.2 In the manufacturing and retail\ntrade sectors, for example, subcontracted employment was reduced by 87 percent and 70 percent,\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 2017,
      "end_char": 2215,
      "text": "respectively, compared to the first quarter of 2021. At the same time, there was no apparent change\nin total employment in these sectors by the end of the third quarter, suggesting that most of the\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2215,
      "end_char": 2429,
      "text": "previously subcontracted workers were rehired as direct employees. The new law, therefore, does\n1 The provision of services considered to be specialized and not part of the core business of the company using these\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2429,
      "end_char": 2625,
      "text": "services remains permitted. Also, services can be provided by entities within the same group.\n2 The law required the transition to be completed by September 1, 2021.\nINTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND 65"
    }
  ]
}

