      "text": "2021Q1 2021Q2 2021Q3 2021Q4 2022Q1 2022Q2\nexpected a similar increase in the value added of Manufacturing Retail trade Support services to businesses (RHS)\nSource:INEGI.\nsector now directly employing the workers.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 848,
      "end_char": 1041,
      "text": "However, provisional data report a broadly stable growth of value added in these sectors, with no\nsubstantial change in the ratio of value added to production yet, suggesting that the standard\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 1041,
      "end_char": 1235,
      "text": "methodology used to compute quarterly national accounts may not yet fully capture the structural\nchange.3 Underlying economic conditions in the second half of 2021 could thus have been stronger\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1235,
      "end_char": 1364,
      "text": "than reported.4 Even so, the pandemic recovery of the Mexican economy would still have been\nrelatively slower compared to peers.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1364,
      "end_char": 1590,
      "text": "3 To ensure timely release, quarterly national accounts provide GDP estimates built on short term indicators like\nproduction indexes, before more comprehensive data are collected, with a pre-defined process and assumptions on\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1590,
      "end_char": 1732,
      "text": "the structure of the economy.\n4 The GDP growth deceleration may also partly reflect the impact of other shocks.\n66 INTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND"
    }
  ]
